      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}\\,$ if $\\,T({b}_{1})=8{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=7{b}_{1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since we have $\\,T({b}_{1})=8{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=7{b}_{1}$, we have\n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
